	•	Section 2 Comments/Quotes: The model was developed in 6,579 adult heart transplant recipients and evaluated in two external cohorts of 1,567 and 1,853 recipients, giving 9,999 participants across development and validation. The intended use was decision support at heart-transplant waitlisting. Age was reported as a median of 57 years rather than a mean, and 72.5% were male; an explicit female percentage was not reported. Race and clinical history were reported, including diabetes, heart-failure diagnosis, previous transplantation, dialysis, mechanical support, renal function, biomarkers, and right-heart catheterization measurements.

