	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Missing predictor values were imputed with a K-nearest-neighbors imputer using K = 50, primarily for right-heart catheterization measurements, BNP, and blood urea nitrogen. Class imbalance was addressed through positive-sample class-weight tuning from 3 to 10, and precision-recall performance was reported for the 13.4% adverse-outcome prevalence. The primary temporal external test cohort contained 1,567 recipients; a second external cohort contained 1,853. Study code or trained model weights were not reported, although the model was implemented as an online calculator.

